# Copy to deploy/.env and edit. Never commit .env.

# The DNS name phones and MCP clients use. Point its A record at this server first.
# A record ONLY, no AAAA: the bundled Compose network is IPv4-only, so IPv6 clients would arrive
# through Docker's userland proxy as one shared address, sharing one login/setup/pairing limit
# (a stranger could lock you out). See docs/server.md, "IPv6 (advanced, untested)".
ORBIT_DOMAIN=orbit.example.com

# Let's Encrypt account email (expiry notices). Required by the Caddyfile.
ACME_EMAIL=you@example.com

# --- Private server on Tailscale (docker-compose.tailscale.yml) ---
# Uncomment BOTH lines below. WARNING: without COMPOSE_FILE, a plain `docker compose up -d`
# uses docker-compose.yml alone and publishes 80/443 on every address of this machine,
# bypassing ufw. With it, every docker compose command run in deploy/ uses the override,
# which publishes 443 on TAILSCALE_IP only. Check with: docker compose ps
# ORBIT_DOMAIN is then the MagicDNS name, e.g. myserver.tail1234.ts.net
# COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.yml:docker-compose.tailscale.yml
# TAILSCALE_IP=100.64.0.1       # this machine's Tailscale IPv4 (tailscale ip -4)
